hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1014","Narrated by Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi, and I read it to Bundar, and this is the hadith of Al-Dawrqi, narrated by Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad bin Jafar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “prayed on the day of the conquest placing his shoe on his left.”"
"1015","We told Bundar, we told Othman bin Omar, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad bin Jaafar, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Sufyan, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Al-Sa'ib said: “I attended the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the year of the conquest, and he prayed on the day of the conquest, took off his shoes and placed them on the ""His left"""
